<hr />
<h2>1. Request #1 Sizing: Two GPU Training Nodes</h2>
<p><strong>Observed ML Baseline:</strong>
- July 2026 (full month): $892.97 [qid:659a87ae] — team "ml"
- August 2026 (partial, through 15th): $414.32 [qid:e0429d85]</p>
<p><strong>Interpretation:</strong> The partial August data cannot be annualized directly. At current run-rate, ML would project to ~$828 for a full August, suggesting seasonal or workload-driven variability rather than structural decline.</p>
<p><strong>Capacity Implication:</strong> Two additional GPU training nodes would expand ML compute capacity significantly. Without explicit per-node cost figures in the data, the request cannot be precisely costed, but any GPU instance type (p3/p4/g4/g5 family) would likely add $500–$2,000/month per node depending on instance size and utilization. <strong>The request requires explicit instance-type specification and utilization assumptions to complete estimation.</strong></p>
